        "0x100210208",
        "0x1002102c8"
      ],
      "claim": "Builder creates explicit fade sections using AudioVolumeCurveStream100110c18, a clone of the saved MInterpolator and per-event Float32 gain on the containing PAudioSegment. Fade-in and fade-out supply different source origins/lengths; fade-out wrapper extent is incremented by5. Exact clipping/overlapping-fade cases and meaning of the extra5 remain to be closed."
    },
    {
      "addresses": [
        "0x100110c18",
        "0x1001113f8"
      ],
      "claim": "Curve stream stores/retains its curve interface at+50 and normalization flag at+58. Open path invokes curve interface+48 with wrapper length and then+50, conditional on first open and supplied flag. This is separate from canonical segment projection."
    },
    {
      "addresses": [
        "0x100110f6c",
        "0x10011100c",
        "0x100111018",
        "0x1001110fc",
        "0x1001112a4"
      ],
      "claim": "Concrete curve-processing virtual+1a8 queries interface+40 at input position and position+100, computes a binary64 slope and fused intercept, and uses fused multiply-add to evaluate piecewise linear gains with100-frame refresh. When block extent approaches wrapper length, short remaining requests use direct interpolator evaluation. Exact update endpoints and read scheduling require authored controls before promotion; arbitrary block-partition invariance is not presumed."
    },
    {
      "addresses": [
        "0x1001111a0",
        "0x100111354",
        "0x100111124",
        "0x1001112d8"
      ],
      "claim": "The inner scalar and vector sample loops promote each Float32 input to Double, multiply by the Double envelope, then round to Float32. This differs from first rounding the envelope to Float32. Event gain remains a separately ordered stage. No clipping is visible in this concrete processing loop."
    }
  ],
